;. /resume_work_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition resume_work
  ;= Continue existing native work
    Bind capture to a raw own-record inspection cell for the original native
    work. Bind sources to guides and provider to the selected interactive
    provider. Author the continuation below or bind a Nenex assignment page as
    source task. This helper keeps its own report
    attempt while operating only through the original work's declared actions.

    ;@ /flow/input capture
    ;= Exact original work selection
    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Action guides and optional Nenex continuation
    ;@ /flow/input provider
    ;= Interactive provider

    ;@ /flow/step grounded ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/work_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind capture capture
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Require native work without replacing its identity

    ;@ /flow/step task ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/agent_task
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Prepare a continuation request

    ;@ /flow/step continued ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/interactive_requests
    ;@ /flow/bind tasks task
    ;@ /flow/bind provider provider
    ;= Use the original work's declared controls

    ;@ /flow/step report ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/report_pages
    ;@ /flow/bind responses continued
    ;= Read the validated continuation report

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages report
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Retain the report and source provenance

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Continuation report

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses native
    ;= Resume this work
      The default assignment is to inspect the selected work and identify its
      next continuation. No effect is authorized until the authored brief or
      bound task names the desired continuation, authorized answer/evidence/
      retry/resume, and observable result. Ask for those missing choices before
      mutation. A bound Nenex task is ordinary current evidence; editing it
      wakes the existing hand and retains previous attempts.

      Start from the captured original work address. Reread its current owner,
      controller or head, context, evidence, holes and resumption links. Keep
      the original work distinct from this helper's request and controller.
      Inspect previous attempts and accepted action receipts before repeating
      any effect. Historical navigation is not current evidence or authority.

      Distinguish active work, missing input, a concrete blocked condition,
      deliberately paused work and a completed result using the native records.
      If work is already running, report its current progress without duplicate
      dispatch. If it is complete, verify the result and report no change.
      Never silently enable paused work, adopt another provider or definition,
      rewrite status, resolve a hole to claim completion, overwrite an attempt,
      or create a replacement controller.

      Discover the original subject's declared controls with shrine_actions.
      Only supply answers, evidence, retries or resumes explicitly authorized
      by the task. Use current expected/displayed/publication fields and the
      declared argument encoding. The host owns invocation identity. Do not
      invent a control, input selection or effect key. After a stale refusal,
      reread and reassess; after uncertain completion, inspect receipts first.

      Missing clarification remains on the existing work hole. Return empty
      source and the exact required input in note when it prevents the requested
      continuation. The caller can update this helper's bound task evidence or
      answer through the original application's declared control. Do not copy
      a hole into another lifecycle or treat the helper's report as an answer
      to the original question.

      Reread affected work and result cells after an accepted action. Admission
      is not completion. Return a Semidoc section with observed status, what
      changed, exact original work/receipt/result references, and remaining
      questions. Preserve all previous attempts, captures and history. If a
      required postcondition is still unverified, leave the helper unresolved.
